Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu | Official Podcast | Episode 2: Bigger & Different
To coincide with Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu’s release on Disney+, we are taking fans behind the scenes with the team that made the movie. In the second and final episode of the podcast, writer-director Jon Favreau sits down with the film's Academy Award winning composer, Ludwig Göransson, to chat about taking the baton from John Williams and creating the film's iconic original music, embraced by legions of Star Wars fans the world over. Jon then wraps up the episode with the second half of his conversation with his friend, co-writer and the president of LucasFilm, Dave Filoni, recounting the many highlights of turning their beloved television series into a blockbuster film.

